<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48150" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">thērĭăcus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θηριακός,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>good against the
				poison of animals</i>, esp. <i>against the bite of
				serpents.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pastilli,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					29, 4, 21, § 70</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vitis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pall. Febr. 28, 1</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">thērĭăca</span></b> ,
			ae, or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-ē</span></b> , ēs, f.,
				<i>an antidote against the bite of serpents</i>,
			or <i>against poison</i> in gen., <i><span class="en">Plin. 20,
				24, 100, § 264</span></i>; <i><span class="en">29, 1, 8, §
			24</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Scrib. Comp. 163</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Tert. Anim. 24</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Hier. adv. Jovin. 2,
		6</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
